# Apache config for the deployed site (Hostinger). Files in public/ are copied
# into dist/ untouched, so this lands at the site root where Apache looks for
# it. Without it a bad URL gets Apache's own plain-text 404 rather than the
# site's page.
#
# The path is absolute so it names the file at the document root, rather than
# a "404.html" relative to whatever directory was requested. Astro builds
# routes as directories (/work/gfm/index.html) but special-cases this one to
# 404.html at the root, which is the name Apache is pointed at here.
ErrorDocument 404 /404.html
